    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d139">

                <pb facs="0184" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">548.G1/104h: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Hamilton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Beck</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-04-29T17:00:00-04:00">April 29, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>15. For Dodds. In view of the possible adverse press and public criticism which
                    may follow the withholding of information as you propose, the Department feels
                    that it is most important that as frank a statement as possible of your
                    recommendations be published immediately after your arrival in this country.</p>
                <p>As the members of both delegations will be together in New York I have instructed
                        Travers<anchor n="44" xml:id="d139-f1"/> to meet you at airport with the
                    thought <pb facs="0185" n="175" xml:id="pg175"/> that a statement may be
                    approved by both delegations and telegraphed to London for concurrence in order
                    Joint statement may be released by both Governments Sunday afternoon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d139-f1" n="44" xml:id="d139-f1-content">
                <p>Howard K. Travers, Chief of the Visa Division.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
